.TH GHOSTLIGHT-MCP-CONNECTOR 1 "2026-09-05" "Ghostlight 1.3.4" "Ghostlight Manual"
.SH NAME
ghostlight-mcp-connector \- Model Context Protocol stdio edge for Ghostlight
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghostlight-mcp-connector
.SH DESCRIPTION
The MCP connector is the stdio edge an MCP client launches. It speaks the Model
Context Protocol on standard input and output and relays to the local
Ghostlight authority over a typed local connection.
.PP
It takes no arguments and is not intended to be run by hand. An MCP client
starts it, and
.BR ghostlight (1)
registers it in that client's configuration.
.PP
The connector owns protocol lifecycle, framing, correlation, cancellation
forwarding, catalog retrieval, and generic rendering. It makes no product
decisions and holds no policy: what Ghostlight will and will not do is decided
by the authority, not here.
.PP
If the local authority is not running, the connector starts the exact sibling
.B ghostlight
executable in its own installation directory, with no arguments, and continues
its ordinary reconnect loop. It never searches PATH and never accepts an
executable path over the wire.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits zero when its client closes the stream. A protocol or transport failure
exits non-zero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ghostlight (1),
.BR ghostlight-browser-connector (1)
